					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-24 | Sunday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://farm2.static.flickr.com/1232/613799739_fae2801778_o.jpg" alt="" width="430" height="128" /><br /><br />Seattle! Pick up a copy of today&#39;s Sunday newpaper to see Geo on the front page. Those out of state can see/save the image by clicking <strong><a href="http://seattletimes.nwsource.com/PDF/frontpage.pdf">HERE</a>. <br /><br /></strong>New York! Catch Blue Scholars in your area this Wednesday. Information is to your right. Go to&nbsp;<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="1" color="#333300"><font face="Arial"><font color="#0000ff"><font size="2">Going.com/BayaniAlbumRelease</font></font></font></font><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="1" color="#333300"><font face="Arial"><font color="#0000ff"><font size="2"> </font></font></font></font>and find out how you can get in for FREE. An all ages performance at Fat Beats earlier on in the day will also be goin down.<br /><br />Beacon Hill! Big up.<br /><br />Peace<br />daps1<br /><br /><br /><strong><br /><br /></strong><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-21 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br>Youth of all ages should check out this show sponsored by Massline, featuring a public showing of Blue Scholars&#39; new video &quot;Back Home&quot; (which looks hella filthy on bigger screens). &quot;Manoj&quot; will also air, which was shown at the Showbox for the first night of the Bayani release party last month. To top if all off, videos made and created by the youth themselves will also be shown. Shouts out to WAPIFASA, Greg, Kirbs, Nam, Ari, Daniel, Tran...all y&#39;all. <br /><br /><img src="http://i19.tinypic.com/6fajolj.jpg" alt="" width="430" height="316" /><br /><br />Enjoy the weather!<br />Peace<br />daps1<br /> <p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-20 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://www.bluescholars.com/images/flyers/kicksclusive.jpg" alt="" width="350" height="349" /><br /><br />Attention: folks in the NYC area! Blue Scholars are back in town on WEDNESDAY, JUNE 27 to make two special apperances to celebrate the release of BAYANI:<br /><br /><strong>WED, JUNE 27,2007<br />BLUE SCHOLARS @ FAT BEATS NYC<br />IN STORE PERFORMANCE</strong><br />FREE | 6pm | All-Ages<br />406 6th Ave 2nd Floor<br />New York, NY 10011<br /><br />and later that evening...<br /><br /><br /><strong>WED, JUNE 27, 2007<br />Rawkus, KEXP.org </strong>and<strong> Kicksclusive Magazine </strong>Present<strong>:<br /></strong><br /><strong>Blue Scholars <br /></strong><br />w/Special Guests <strong>Cause  </strong>and<strong> DJ Yamez<br />@ Sol </strong><br />609 29th Street<br />Between 11th and West Side Highway<br />New York, NY<br />21 and Over |  9pm<br />FREE if you RSVP AT Going.com/BayaniAlbumRelease<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-19 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br><strong>RIP Vincent Chin<br />1955-1982<br /></strong><br />Today marks the 25th anniversary of <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vincent_Chin" target="_blank">Vincent Chin</a>&#39;s beating and subsequent murder. The incident is referenced in the second verse of <em>&quot;Morning of America&quot;</em> (track #14 on <em>Bayani</em>). Many incidents of racially-motivated violence against Asians in America have occurred before and since June 19, 1982 but Chin&#39;s murder stands as a monumental injustice - the two Detroit men who beat Chin to death admitted and even boasted about it and were acquitted of all charges. Check the 1989 Academy Award-nominated documentary &quot;Who Killed Vincent Chin?&quot; for some insight. <br /><br /><br /><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-15 | Friday</font></strong><br><br>Peace to all who came through the <strong>Portland Music Millennium</strong> (23rd) last night to celebrate Bayani release week. Word is they&#39;re flying off the shelves in the Seattle and Portland areas, so pick one up now if you don&#39;t want to wait for the re-order shipment. Bayani is also currently (as of this morning) #10 on the iTunes hip-hop chart and #20 on the Amazon.com hip-hop chart. The support has been massive. For those who need a break from bumping the album, check out this essay on <a href="http://www.massline.info/frso/amlsfso.htm">THE MASS LINE</a> (the revolutionary concept and practice, not the record label). <br /><br />And don&#39;t forget: tonight and tomorrow at Langston Hughes Performing Arts Center - Massline presents The New Seattle Orchestra (see below). Your boy <strong>Sabzi</strong> hosts tonight with <strong>Hari Kondabolu</strong>. And that&#39;s not it. <strong>Gabriel Teodros</strong> and <strong>RA Scion</strong> will also be blessing the mic! Then he and I roll to the <strong>Bellevue Silver Platters at 2PM</strong> tomorrow and then roll to the <strong>China Clipper in Olympia</strong> for a KAOS benefit show. Come through people.<br /><br />isulong!<br />Geo<br /><br />-------------<br /><br /><strong>The New Seattle Orchestra <br />@ Langston Hughes Performing Arts Center<br />Fri. &amp; Sat - June 15th and 16th</strong><br />8pm All Ages<br /><br /><blockquote>For 2 nights at the Langston Hughes Center for Performing Arts we are pulling out all of the stops and presenting The New Seattle Orchestra, a 20+ piece orchestra consisting of some of the most innovative performers in Seattle including Paul Rucker, Izaak Mills, Owour Arunga, Dylan Rieck, D&#39;Vonne Lewis, Jacques Willis, Eric Peters, Beth Fleenor and many others performing the works of Evan Flory-Barnes and Ahamefule J. Oluo with special guests of RA Scion of Common Market and Gabriel Teodros who will be performing with the orchestra. Comedian Hari Kondabolu and Sabzi (Blue Scholars, Common Market) will be hosting this event. This will be a night to remember!<br /></blockquote><br /><em>Langston Hughes Center for Performing Arts<br />104 17th Ave S. Seattle, WA 98144</em><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> [29] <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=245">[50]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=250">[51]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=255">[52]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=260">[53]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=265">[54]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=270">[55]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=275">[56]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=280">[57]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=285">[58]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=290">[59]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[&gt;&gt;]</A>  </span></p>
